stunt driver Chris Joe is about to drive  over a bridge in the Chinese city of  Suzhou it's not an ordinary bridge  designed by artist Steve mesm it's a  bridge made of sheets of paper and  absolutely nothing else this can't be  possible  you would find me driving across  anything like that this is awesome  yes it is amazing we caught up with  Steve in his studio in England to see  how he built his paper bridge and then  we have the formwork in the middle this  is exactly the same paper that we used  in China it's just red and then we just  stack the paper from both sides at the  same time when we come up to the middle  then we take the chocks away from down  the bottom and we can just slide it out  and then the arch will just stay on but  how can flimsy sheets of paper support  the weight of a car if you're going to  build a bridge out of paper and you're  not going to use any other materials  like cables or glue and arch is  definitely the way to go it arced like  this all the pieces are angled so that  gravity pulls them into each other so  the pieces on the side are wanting to  fall in towards the center but the  pieces in the center are pushing back so  everything just gets locked into place  but the ends of the bridge there are two  abutments and they stop the bridge from  actually splaying out with and a result  is a very strong structure
 

